# P23 on GtkBackend on macOS (TEST_BACKEND=gtk4), #125: a click on a row must move the selection -- proved on the screen.
# Measured 2026-10-16 from p23-macos-gtk4-final-20261016-013837.png (1640x1296, halved to 820x648; origin=frame, 28 pt native title bar, geometry frame=(550,184) client=(550,212)). Nothing in the file changes the layout, so the capture is the layout every click meets.
# The AppKit file's Select row 2 click (y 231) fell above its button (frame y 236-270), and the row click at (100,558) landed on row 4 (y 540-567) instead of row 5 (y about 581) on GTK's layout (gtk4-aim-20261016.csv2).
# After this file: selected row: 4 with row 5 highlighted. If row 5 is on target and still nothing is selected, GTK Table click-to-select is the defect, not the aim.
# macOS 上 GtkBackend 的 P23:Select row 2 與第 5 列依 GTK 擷圖重新量測，結束時 selected row: 4。
sleep,,,,,,700000,let the window settle,macos
click,73,253,frame,left,,,Select row 2 (was 67;231 above the button) -- the framework puts the highlight on index 2,macos
sleep,,,,,,700000,let the highlight be drawn,macos
click,100,581,frame,left,,,"row 5 (was 100;558 on row 4) -- the capture must read selected row: 4 with row 5 highlighted",macos
sleep,,,,,,900000,let the readout redraw before the capture,macos
